## Installation
------

### npm

Install Owl Carousel 3 in an npm project:

```bash
npm install owlcarousel3
```
The package declares jQuery `>=1.8.3 <5` as a peer dependency. npm 7 and newer install a compatible jQuery version automatically when your project does not already provide one.

### CDN

Use versioned jsDelivr URLs when loading the prebuilt files without npm:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/owlcarousel3@{{ pkg.version }}/dist/assets/owl.carousel.min.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/owlcarousel3@{{ pkg.version }}/dist/assets/owl.theme.default.min.css">

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/jquery@4.0.0/dist/jquery.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/owlcarousel3@{{ pkg.version }}/dist/owl.carousel.min.js"></script>
```

### Include CSS
First, include two CSS files into your HTML head:
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="owlcarousel/owl.carousel.min.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="owlcarousel/owl.theme.default.min.css">
```
> `owl.carousel.css` file is required and should be included before any *.js files.


Second `owl.theme.default.css` file is optional and feel free to edit it. However, it is required if you'd like the default nav controls like dots or next buttons.
The npm package also contains the [SCSS](https://sass-lang.com/) source for custom builds and themes.


### Include JS

When using local files, include jQuery followed by `owl.carousel.min.js` near the end of the page.

```html
<script src="jquery.min.js"></script>
<script src="owlcarousel/owl.carousel.min.js"></script>
```

### Set HTML

You don't need any special markup. All you need is to wrap your divs(owl works with any type element a/img/span..) inside the container element `<div class="owl-carousel">`.
Class "owl-carousel" is mandatory to apply proper styles that come from owl.carousel.css file. If you want the default nav controls like dots or buttons, you must also include the "owl-theme" class on that same div.

```html
<!-- Set up your HTML -->
<div class="owl-carousel">
  <div> Your Content </div>
  <div> Your Content </div>
  <div> Your Content </div>
  <div> Your Content </div>
  <div> Your Content </div>
  <div> Your Content </div>
  <div> Your Content </div>
</div>
```

### Call the plugin

Now call the Owl initializer function and your carousel is ready.

```javascript
$(document).ready(function(){
  $(".owl-carousel").owlCarousel();
});
```
> See [demos](../demos/demos.html) for customisation and options usage.

